title: Preserve finality during state recovery and sparse warp checkpoint import
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Restoring state for existing canonical headers preserves the finalized chain head and persists the restored-state cursor across restart.
    State replay rechecks committed and staged finality before writing, so a competing finalized branch cannot leave a stale-fork recovery checkpoint.
    The first finalized warp checkpoint can be imported when retained proof headers have incomplete ancestry. The missing-history gap remains available for backfill.
crates:
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: patch
- name: sc-service
  bump: patch
- name: sc-consensus-grandpa
  bump: none
- name: sc-service-test
  bump: none
- name: substrate-test-runtime
  bump: none
